msgid "设备与控制组文件系统"
msgstr "Device and control group filesystems"

msgid "devtmpfs"
msgstr "devtmpfs"

msgid ""
"``mount(\"devtmpfs\", target, \"devtmpfs\", flags, data)`` 挂载内核维护的设备节点。 "
"所有挂载共享同一内存文件系统及节点元数据，每个挂载分别维护 ``nodev``、 ``nosuid``、``noexec`` "
"等挂载点策略。普通文件、目录、符号链接及用户创建的 设备节点使用现有 VFS 权限检查。设备打开按 inode 的类型和 ``st_rdev`` "
"分派到驱动，``nodev`` 挂载拒绝打开设备。"
msgstr ""
"``mount(\"devtmpfs\", target, \"devtmpfs\", flags, data)`` mounts the "
"kernel-maintained device nodes. All mounts share the same in-memory "
"filesystem and node metadata. Each mount retains its own mountpoint "
"policies, including ``nodev``, ``nosuid``, and ``noexec``. Regular files,"
" directories, symlinks, and user-created device nodes use the existing "
"VFS permission checks. Device opens are dispatched to drivers by inode "
"type and ``st_rdev``; a ``nodev`` mount rejects device opens."

msgid "设备生命周期"
msgstr "Device lifecycle"

msgid ""
"设备注册、注销及分区变化通知 VFS worker 合并更新。首次挂载同步生成完整 设备清单。后续更新保留已有设备的 "
"``chmod``、``chown``，并尊重用户删除、 替换和占用的名称。设备移除只删除仍由内核持有的原 inode，非空目录保留。 "
"内存不足时保留已发布节点与待重试状态。最后一个公开挂载卸载后，私有 backing 继续保留，后续挂载可看到原有内容及权限。"
msgstr ""
"Device registration, removal, and partition changes notify the VFS "
"worker, which coalesces updates. The first mount synchronously populates "
"the complete device inventory. Later updates retain ``chmod`` and "
"``chown`` changes and respect names removed, replaced, or occupied by "
"users. Device removal deletes only the original inode still owned by the "
"kernel; nonempty directories remain. If memory runs out, published nodes "
"remain and the update stays pending for retry. The private backing "
"filesystem survives the last public unmount, so later mounts see the same"
" contents and permissions."

msgid ""
"设备默认归 root，权限为 ``0600``。``null``、``zero``、``full``、``random``、 "
"``urandom``、``tty`` 和 ``ptmx`` 为 ``0666``。``fd``、``stdin``、``stdout``、 "
"``stderr`` 使用指向 ``/proc/self/fd`` 及对应描述符的符号链接。 ``pts`` 和 ``shm`` "
"提供独立文件系统的挂载目录。"
msgstr ""
"Devices default to root ownership and mode ``0600``. ``null``, ``zero``, "
"``full``, ``random``, ``urandom``, ``tty``, and ``ptmx`` use mode "
"``0666``. ``fd``, ``stdin``, ``stdout``, and ``stderr`` are symlinks to "
"``/proc/self/fd`` and the corresponding descriptors. ``pts`` and ``shm`` "
"provide mountpoints for separate filesystems."

msgid "devtmpfs 挂载选项"
msgstr "devtmpfs mount options"

msgid ""
"挂载数据使用 tmpfs 的 ``mode``、``uid``、``gid``、``size``、``nr_blocks`` 和 "
"``nr_inodes`` 语法。私有 backing 初始为 ``mode=0755,size=0,nr_inodes=0``。 "
"重新配置先验证整个选项集，再原子提交容量和超级块策略。``mode``、``uid``、 ``gid`` 只在首次创建 tmpfs 时设置根 "
"inode。已有无限容量的实例拒绝追溯增加 容量上限，已有内容也必须容纳在新上限内，与 Linux shmem 的重新配置约束一致。"
msgstr ""
"Mount data uses the tmpfs syntax for ``mode``, ``uid``, ``gid``, "
"``size``, ``nr_blocks``, and ``nr_inodes``. The private backing "
"filesystem starts with ``mode=0755,size=0,nr_inodes=0``. Reconfiguration "
"validates the whole option set before atomically committing capacity and "
"superblock policy. ``mode``, ``uid``, and ``gid`` set the root inode only"
" at initial tmpfs creation. An existing unlimited instance cannot "
"retroactively acquire a limit, and existing contents must fit under any "
"new limit, matching Linux shmem reconfiguration constraints."

msgid "devpts"
msgstr "devpts"

msgid ""
"``mount(\"devpts\", target, \"devpts\", flags, data)`` 每次创建独立实例，通常挂在 "
"``/dev/pts``。每个实例有自己的 ``st_dev``、``ptmx`` 和从 0 开始的从端编号； "
"绑定挂载保留原实例。``statfs`` 报告 ``0x1cd1``，``/proc/filesystems`` 将其列为 ``nodev`` "
"文件系统。打开 ``ptmx`` 后，``TIOCGPTN`` 返回本实例的编号； ``TIOCSPTLCK`` 解锁后才能打开对应从端。"
msgstr ""
"Each ``mount(\"devpts\", target, \"devpts\", flags, data)`` creates a "
"separate instance, normally at ``/dev/pts``. Each instance has its own "
"``st_dev``, ``ptmx``, and slave numbering starting at 0. Bind mounts "
"retain the original instance. ``statfs`` reports ``0x1cd1``, and "
"``/proc/filesystems`` lists devpts as a ``nodev`` filesystem. After "
"opening ``ptmx``, ``TIOCGPTN`` returns the number in that instance. Use "
"``TIOCSPTLCK`` to unlock the slave before opening it."

msgid ""
"从端报告字符设备号 ``136:<编号>``，但打开时以实际实例和 inode 身份为准，复制 "
"设备号创建的节点不会连接到该终端。``/proc/<pid>/stat`` 中的控制终端设备号也 使用实例内编号；固定虚拟终端仍使用主设备号 4。"
msgstr ""
"The slave reports character device number ``136:<number>``, but opening "
"it uses the actual instance and inode identity. A node created with a "
"copy of the number will not connect to that terminal. The controlling "
"terminal device number in ``/proc/<pid>/stat`` also uses the instance-"
"local number. Fixed virtual terminals still use major number 4."

msgid "devpts 挂载选项"
msgstr "devpts mount options"

msgid ""
"``uid=``、``gid=``：新从端的十进制所有者；未指定时使用创建 PTY 的进程的 ``fsuid``、``fsgid``。根目录和 "
"``ptmx`` 归挂载者，根目录初始权限为 ``0755``。"
msgstr ""
"``uid=`` and ``gid=`` set the decimal owner IDs for new slaves. When "
"omitted, they default to the PTY creator's ``fsuid`` and ``fsgid``. The "
"mounter owns the root directory and ``ptmx``. The root directory starts "
"with mode ``0755``."

msgid ""
"``mode=``、``ptmxmode=``：八进制权限，最多保留 ``07777``。默认从端为 ``0600``、``ptmx`` 为 "
"``0000``。若直接通过符号链接或绑定挂载打开 ``ptmx``， 可用 ``ptmxmode=0666`` 或相应的 ``chmod`` "
"让非特权用户访问。"
msgstr ""
"``mode=`` and ``ptmxmode=`` take octal permissions and retain bits "
"through ``07777``. The slave defaults to ``0600`` and ``ptmx`` to "
"``0000``. For direct access to ``ptmx`` through a symlink or bind mount, "
"use ``ptmxmode=0666`` or the equivalent ``chmod`` to grant access to "
"unprivileged users."

msgid ""
"``max=``：实例内保留的 PTY 数量上限，范围为 0 到 1048576。默认不额外限制 内部 PTY 资源。达到上限时，新建返回 "
"``ENOSPC``。"
msgstr ""
"``max=`` caps reserved PTYs per instance, from 0 to 1048576. By default "
"no additional limit is applied to internal PTY resources. Creating a PTY "
"at the limit fails with ``ENOSPC``."

msgid "``newinstance``：兼容选项，可以省略。忽略逗号之间的空字段。"
msgstr ""
"``newinstance`` is accepted for compatibility and may be omitted. Empty "
"fields between commas are ignored."

msgid ""
"重新挂载从默认值解析选项。成功后立即更新 ``ptmx`` 权限和挂载策略；新选项 只改变以后创建的从端，不重置已有从端的权限或所有者。降低 "
"``max`` 不会强制 关闭已有会话。未通过验证的选项不会改变现有配置或挂载策略。标记 ``nodev`` 的挂载点不能用来直接打开设备。"
msgstr ""
"Remount parses options from their defaults. On success it updates "
"``ptmx`` permissions and mount policy immediately. New options affect "
"only future slaves and do not reset existing slave permissions or "
"ownership. Lowering ``max`` does not forcibly close sessions. Options "
"that fail validation leave the configuration and mount policy unchanged. "
"A mountpoint marked ``nodev`` cannot be used to open devices directly."

msgid "编号与卸载"
msgstr "Numbering and unmounting"

msgid ""
"最后一个主端关闭时，从端名称被移除，仍打开的从端收到挂断通知。仍有端点引用 的会话继续占用编号和 ``max`` 配额；只剩 ``O_PATH``"
" 等元数据引用时则可以重用 公开编号。旧的从端 inode 与新会话不同：仍可读取旧 inode 的元数据（链接数为 0），尝试再次打开设备返回 "
"``EIO``。正常卸载时仍被打开的路径或端点引用会令 挂载忙（``EBUSY``）；释放引用后可以卸载。"
msgstr ""
"Closing the last master unlinks the slave name and notifies still-open "
"slave endpoints of a hangup. Sessions with endpoint references still "
"reserve their number and count against ``max``. If only metadata "
"references such as ``O_PATH`` remain, the public number can be reused. "
"The old slave inode is distinct from the new session: its metadata "
"remains readable (with a link count of 0), but opening it as a device "
"again fails with ``EIO``. Open paths or endpoints make a normal unmount "
"fail with ``EBUSY`` until the references are released."

msgid ""
"打开传统字符设备 ``5:2`` 时，内核从该设备实际所在的目录查找同级 ``pts/ptmx``。找到 devpts "
"后，新会话及主端描述符属于该实例，传统设备本身的 权限决定是否可打开。找不到有效的 devpts 多路复用器时沿用启动阶段的旧 PTY "
"分配；其他查找错误则返回调用方。"
msgstr ""
"When opening legacy character device ``5:2``, the kernel looks for "
"sibling ``pts/ptmx`` under the actual directory that contains the device."
" If it finds devpts, the new session and master descriptor belong to that"
" instance, while access depends on the permissions of the legacy device "
"node. If no valid devpts multiplexer is found, the kernel uses its early-"
"boot PTY allocation path. Other lookup errors are returned to the caller."

msgid "cgroup v2"
msgstr "Unified cgroup hierarchy (v2)"

msgid ""
"``mount(\"none\", \"/sys/fs/cgroup\", \"cgroup2\", flags, data)`` "
"挂载统一控制组层级。 ``/proc/filesystems`` 将其列为 ``nodev``，``statfs`` 返回 "
"``0x63677270``。 所有挂载共享同一层级和 inode 身份，包括最后一次卸载后的重新挂载；只读等挂载点 策略独立。管理员可以用 "
"``mkdir`` 创建控制组，用 ``rmdir`` 删除没有活任务和 子组的非根组。"
msgstr ""
"``mount(\"none\", \"/sys/fs/cgroup\", \"cgroup2\", flags, data)`` mounts "
"the unified control group hierarchy. ``/proc/filesystems`` lists it as "
"``nodev`` and ``statfs`` reports ``0x63677270``. Mounts share a hierarchy"
" and inode identities, even after the last attachment is unmounted and "
"mounted again. Each attachment has its own policy, including read-only. "
"An administrator can create a group with ``mkdir`` and remove a non-root "
"group with no live tasks or children using ``rmdir``."

msgid "成员与事件"
msgstr "Membership and events"

msgid ""
"向 ``cgroup.procs`` 写入 PID 或 TID 会迁移该进程的所有活线程，不迁移子进程； 写入 0 "
"选择调用者。读取该文件列出本组的进程 ID；只读的 ``cgroup.threads`` 列出本组的线程 "
"ID。``/proc/<pid>/cgroup`` 以 ``0::/路径`` 报告成员身份， 不依赖控制组层级挂载在何处。只有拥有 "
"``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` 的用户任务能修改层级和控制值。"
msgstr ""
"Writing a PID or TID to ``cgroup.procs`` moves every live thread in that "
"process, but not its child processes. Writing 0 selects the caller. "
"Reading that file lists process IDs in the group; the read-only "
"``cgroup.threads`` lists thread IDs. ``/proc/<pid>/cgroup`` reports "
"membership as ``0::/path`` regardless of where the hierarchy is mounted. "
"Only user tasks with ``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` can modify the hierarchy and its "
"controls."

msgid ""
"非根组的 ``cgroup.events`` 中，``populated`` 表示本组或后代是否仍有活线程， 不包含僵尸。其变化与 "
"``pids.events``、``pids.events.local`` 的变化由 VFS worker 合并后发出 inotify "
"``IN_MODIFY``。被删除的组或已停用的控制器文件不再接受读写； 保留的 inode "
"不会指向后来创建的同名组或文件。仍保留成员引用的僵尸显示 `` (deleted)`` 后缀。"
msgstr ""
"The ``populated`` field in a non-root group’s ``cgroup.events`` reports "
"live threads in the group or its descendants, excluding zombies. The VFS "
"worker coalesces changes to this field and the ``pids.events`` and "
"``pids.events.local`` counters before emitting inotify ``IN_MODIFY``. "
"Retired group and controller files no longer accept reads or writes. A "
"retained inode never resolves to a new group or file with the same name. "
"Zombies retaining membership in a removed group show a `` (deleted)`` "
"suffix."

msgid "PID 配额"
msgstr "PID limits"

msgid ""
"``pids`` 是唯一支持的控制器。向 ``cgroup.subtree_control`` 写 ``+pids``， 可为直接子组启用 "
"``pids.max``、``pids.current``、``pids.peak`` 和事件计数。 "
"非根组必须先从父组继承控制器，才能向下启用。已经向下启用的控制器须从下往上停用。 ``pids.max`` 默认为 "
"``max``。降低上限或迁移线程可以使计数超过上限；以后创建的 线程若超过本组或祖先的上限，则返回 ``EAGAIN``。"
msgstr ""
"``pids`` is the only supported controller. Writing ``+pids`` to "
"``cgroup.subtree_control`` enables ``pids.max``, ``pids.current``, "
"``pids.peak`` and the event counters for direct children. A non-root "
"group can enable it only after receiving it from its parent. Disable an "
"enabled controller from the bottom up. ``pids.max`` defaults to ``max``. "
"Lowering a limit or migrating threads can put a group over its limit; "
"subsequent thread creation returns ``EAGAIN`` if it would exceed the "
"group’s limit or an ancestor’s limit."

msgid ""
"配额按照线程计数，且只在创建成功时计入。普通线程退出后释放其配额；可等待的 僵尸仍计入 ``pids.current``，直至实际回收。带 "
"``WNOWAIT`` 的等待不回收配额。 ``pids.events.local`` 记录本组触发的拒绝，``pids.events`` "
"还累计后代的拒绝。"
msgstr ""
"Each thread is charged only after successful creation. Non-waitable "
"threads release the charge on exit; waitable zombies remain in "
"``pids.current`` until reaped. A wait with ``WNOWAIT`` does not release "
"the charge. ``pids.events.local`` records denials triggered by the "
"group’s own limit, and ``pids.events`` also includes denials triggered in"
" descendants."

msgid ""
"不支持 cgroup v1、threaded 模式、cgroup namespace、非特权委托或其他控制器。 "
"``nsdelegate``、``memory_recursiveprot`` 只接受为兼容性挂载参数，不启用相应功能。 通知仅支持 "
"inotify，不支持通过 ``POLLPRI`` 订阅状态变化。"
msgstr ""
"cgroup v1, threaded mode, cgroup namespaces, unprivileged delegation and "
"other controllers are not supported. ``nsdelegate`` and "
"``memory_recursiveprot`` are accepted only as compatibility mount "
"options; they do not enable those features. Notifications use inotify; "
"state changes are not available through ``POLLPRI``."

msgid "验证范围"
msgstr "Validation scope"

msgid ""
"``tools/test_mount_backend.py`` 覆盖 devtmpfs 共享挂载、元数据、设备号、符号 "
"链接、设备增删、用户替换、挂载策略和内存不足重试，也验证 devpts 实例隔离、 "
"选项、绑定、端点生命周期、编号回收及失败回滚。``tools/test_linux_pty.py`` 覆盖 PTY "
"ABI、会话与主端挂断行为。控制组挂载、文件语义及 inotify 也由 ``tools/test_mount_backend.py`` "
"覆盖；``tools/test_cgroup_scheduler.py`` 检查真实 调度器的配额拒绝、创建回滚、退出及回收。来宾启动、udev "
"和 systemd 集成需要 另行验证。"
msgstr ""
"``tools/test_mount_backend.py`` checks shared devtmpfs mounts, metadata, "
"device numbers, symlinks, device lifecycle, user replacements, mount "
"policy and retry after allocation failure. It also checks devpts "
"isolation, options, bind mounts, endpoint lifetime, number reuse and "
"rollback. ``tools/test_linux_pty.py`` checks the PTY ABI, sessions and "
"master hangup. The mount backend suite covers cgroup mounts, control "
"files and inotify. ``tools/test_cgroup_scheduler.py`` exercises quota "
"denials, creation rollback, exit and reap through the real scheduler. "
"Guest boot, udev and systemd integration require separate validation."
